{"timestamp": "2026-03-02T19:19:24Z", "session_id": "session-20260302-closeout", "signal": ".claude/commands/ drifted from templates/commands/ \u2014 17/23 skills were stale after Session 11 slimdown. Claude was running old wai.md (808b stub) that called the deleted wai-briefing.sh. Root cause: .claude/commands/ is a separate copy, not a symlink.", "impact": 9, "rationale": "Skills served to the agent must match the canonical source. Any skill update to templates/commands/ must be immediately synced to .claude/commands/. Consider adding a sync-commands step to wai-shipit or making .claude/commands/ symlinks.", "by": "claude-sonnet-4-6", "tags": ["framework", "commands-sync", "drift"]}
{"timestamp": "2026-03-02T19:19:24Z", "session_id": "session-20260302-closeout", "signal": "Hook scripts written on Windows (CRLF) fail on WSL2 bash with exit code 2 and cryptic $'\\r' errors. The E2E hook tests caught this correctly.", "impact": 8, "rationale": "Template hook distribution must strip CRLF. Add to wai-ide-setup.md: 'If hook exits with code 2, run: sed -i s/\\r// .claude/hooks/user-prompt-submit.sh'", "by": "claude-sonnet-4-6", "tags": ["hook", "crlf", "windows", "wsl2"]}
{"timestamp": "2026-03-14T07:42:17Z", "session_id": "session-20260314-fleet-upgrade", "signal": "Fleet-wide spoke upgrade executed: 12 spokes upgraded to framework 2.0.18 via bootstrap/spoke-upgrade.sh. Established wheel.framework_version as separate field from wheel.version. WAI-Lugs.jsonl canonical location confirmed as WAI-Spoke/. Three script bugs found and fixed during rollout (git add fatal on missing files, lugs at wrong path, commit step failing silently).", "impact": 9, "rationale": "First fleet-wide coordinated upgrade. Proved the pull-based distribution model works. Established patterns for future upgrades. Every spoke now has hub connection, skills, hooks, and bootstrap files.", "by": "Claude Opus 4.6"}
{"timestamp": "2026-03-14T07:42:17Z", "session_id": "session-20260314-fleet-upgrade", "signal": "Test bench validation caught 3 blocking issues in bootstrap prompt before deployment: wheel.version corruption, CLAUDE.md project content loss, missing .claude/settings.json. Two-stage testing (framework clone + real spoke) proved essential \u2014 Stage 2 found issues invisible from Stage 1.", "impact": 8, "rationale": "Validates the test bench as a required quality gate for any artifact that touches spokes.", "by": "Claude Opus 4.6"}
{"timestamp":"2026-03-14T19:00:00Z","session_id":"session-20260314-fleet-upgrade","signal":"PEV fields (perceive/execute/verify) and pre-closeout dogfooding driven into framework lug advisor and closeout skills. PEV required on all actionable lugs. Dogfooding validates lugs for self-containment before commit. Both propagate to spokes via upgrade.","impact":9,"rationale":"Sub-agent dogfood test revealed 8/17 lugs were unworkable without conversation context. PEV gives cold agents a runway. Dogfooding catches gaps before they ship. Together they close the quality loop on the lug system.","by":"claude-opus-4-6"}
{"timestamp": "2026-03-14T20:00:00Z", "session_id": "session-20260314-200000", "signal": "Hub framework symlink must point to teachings/ folder only — not the entire framework repo. Full-repo symlink creates data pollution risk and breaks the separation between framework internals and distributable teachings.", "impact": 9, "rationale": "Architecture decision affecting all spokes and how the hub accesses framework content. Canonicalizes the teachings/ folder as the only public interface of the framework repo.", "by": "Claude Sonnet 4.6"}
{"timestamp": "2026-03-14T20:00:00Z", "session_id": "session-20260314-200000", "signal": "Dogfood subagent pattern validated: a naive agent reviewing protocol changes caught 4 critical implementation bugs (path mismatch, undefined build process, missing directory creation, unimplementable HMAC) that the authoring agent normalized over. Plan→Epic→Dogfood→Execute is now a mandatory protocol for multi-file changes.", "impact": 9, "rationale": "Meta-protocol that improves quality of all future framework changes. The dogfood subagent acts as a forcing function for self-contained, unambiguous protocol documentation.", "by": "Claude Sonnet 4.6"}
{"timestamp":"2026-03-14T10:00:00Z","session_id":"session-20260314-0903","signal":"Core collaboration working agreement established: plan → create epic lug (announce name) → dogfood via minimal agent → show result → iterate → closeout+restart. Captures the full loop including naming convention and dogfood gate before human review.","impact":9,"rationale":"Fundamental change to how AI-human collaboration works in this project. Every future plan follows this protocol. Saved in taste.spoke.yaml (taste-collab-001) and MEMORY.md.","by":"Claude Sonnet 4.6"}
{"timestamp":"2026-03-14T10:00:00Z","session_id":"session-20260314-0903","signal":"Track verify criteria based on file/directory existence are insufficient — all three verify conditions for track-encapsulation were pre-satisfied on disk while the behavioral protocol was never implemented. Verify criteria must test behavioral adoption, not just artifact presence.","impact":8,"rationale":"Affects how all future epics write their verify fields. Existence checks are necessary but not sufficient for behavioral protocols.","by":"Claude Sonnet 4.6"}
{"timestamp":"2026-03-14T10:00:00Z","session_id":"session-20260314-0903","signal":"Hub /framework/ symlink already serves Step 3a teaching discovery — no hub/broadcast/teachings/latest/ path needed. The symlink hub/framework -> ../framework/teachings/ is the distribution mechanism. Step 3a works correctly with the current hub layout.","impact":8,"rationale":"Closes a false architectural concern. Prevents future effort spent creating broadcast/ scaffolding that isn't needed.","by":"Claude Sonnet 4.6"}
{"timestamp":"2026-03-14T10:18:00Z","session_id":"session-20260314-1012","signal":"Framework spoke now has local WAI-Spoke/commands/wai.md with full 10-step wakeup protocol (installed from Gemini teaching). Steps 3a/5a/5b/5c/9 active: auto-teaching discovery, session track resume/recovery, taste file loading, historian threshold, session track init.","impact":8,"rationale":"This is a significant protocol upgrade — the spoke now participates fully in the track encapsulation system on every wakeup.","by":"Claude Sonnet 4.6"}
{"timestamp":"2026-03-14T11:20:00Z","session_id":"session-20260314-1012","signal":"wai-improve v1.0 shipped — improvement idea protocol with six-step pipeline (load context, intake, fit check, refine, score, promote). Core design validated by two independent reviewers (Opus + GPT). Key pattern: separate challenge from hypothesis — challenges are stable, hypotheses go stale. Fit check against open lugs + existing skills + signals is mandatory before any lug creation. Phase-gated scoring uses current_phase to adjust priority.","impact":8,"rationale":"First formal protocol for managing improvement ideas in Wheelwright. Establishes the intake-to-build pipeline that all future improvement work will flow through.","by":"Claude Sonnet 4.6"}
{"timestamp": "2026-03-15T01:05:00Z", "session_id": "session-20260315-0029", "signal": "core-protocol established: Plan \u2192 Epic \u2192 Dogfood \u2192 Execute. Any change touching 2+ files or 6+ steps requires: (1) written plan, (2) epic lug authored, (3) naive subagent receives full lug + full file content and stress-tests for ambiguity, (4) iterate until clean, (5) explicit user approval before execution. Supersedes complexity-advisor bare 'PLAN ACCEPTED' shorthand. Exception: independent parallel changes (same operation class on N files) are a single logical unit. Rejection reasons and iteration history maintained in lug review_log. Lug id: decision-plan-dogfood-execute-protocol.", "impact": 9, "rationale": "Governs all complex multi-file work across all sessions and models. The dogfood step is the core value \u2014 a naive agent receiving the plan plus file content will surface gaps that the authoring agent normalizes over. Plans that survive dogfood are self-contained and portable across sessions.", "by": "Claude Sonnet 4.6", "lug_ref": "decision-plan-dogfood-execute-protocol"}
{"timestamp": "2026-03-15T01:30:00Z", "session_id": "session-20260315-0029", "signal": "Closeout now automatically distributes new signals as teaching files (Step 9b). old_last_closeout captured at procedure start before Step 5 overwrites it. Condition: hub connected + signals newer than old_last_closeout. Idempotency guard on receiving spoke. Full /wai-teach remains manual for template distribution. Teaching file: closeout-absorbs-signal-teach-v1.md.teaching.", "impact": 8, "rationale": "Removes the last manual step from the standard session flow. Signal distribution is now automatic at every closeout with zero extra commands.", "by": "Claude Sonnet 4.6"}
{"timestamp":"2026-03-15T02:30:00Z","session_id":"session-20260315-0151","signal":"wai-improve Step 6c replaced with structured three-part dogfood audit (Perceive/Execute/Verify), each with explicit pass/fail criteria. No longer conversational. Reframed from standalone skill proposal — folded directly into existing skill.","impact":8,"rationale":"Protocol change affecting every plan approval across all spokes. Structured criteria make dogfood check consistent and auditable rather than judgment-dependent. Teaching file needs updating to distribute change.","by":"Claude Sonnet 4.6"}
{"timestamp":"2026-03-16T00:45:00Z","session_id":"session-20260316-0011","signal":"Historian pattern-scan activity_filter_exclude: 22-token blocklist added to filter protocol-routine activity[] phrases before Jaccard similarity scan. First pass found 30/40 clusters were noise from 'committed', 'updated', 'copied' etc. Filter applied only to activity[] field — open[] and decisions[] unfiltered. Eliminates calibration noise from all future pattern-scan runs across all spokes.","impact":8,"rationale":"Pattern-scan quality was severely degraded by maintenance-routine phrases that appear in nearly every session. This fix makes the scan signal-to-noise ratio viable for long-term use.","by":"Claude Sonnet 4.6"}
{"timestamp":"2026-03-16T00:45:01Z","session_id":"session-20260316-0011","signal":"Shipit production release intent: wai-shipit.md now asks 'Is this a production release?' as Step 0 before any other action. If yes: all 10 steps run normally, then Step 9b applies git tag v{version} + push tag. If no: all 10 steps run identically, no tag. This distinguishes stable releases (cloners can target tags) from quality-gated progress saves (mid-state commits). Minimal protocol addition — no existing steps changed.","impact":8,"rationale":"Without this distinction, every shipit commit looks identical to cloners. Git tags are the standard mechanism for marking stable releases and should be explicit, not implicit.","by":"Claude Sonnet 4.6"}
{"timestamp":"2026-03-16T05:35:00Z","session_id":"session-20260316-0510","signal":"Teaching adoption protocol: safe_to_auto_adopt:true now uses Path A (brief compact table + duplicate check + direct adopt, no ceremony). safe_to_auto_adopt:false retains full mailroom ceremony (Path B). Signal filenames now include sender: signal-YYYYMMDD-HHMM-from-{spoke_id}.md.teaching. Duplicate check on signal type: compare timestamp against existing WAI-Signals.jsonl entries before appending — validated live (both session-31 teachings already present, correctly skipped).","impact":8,"rationale":"The mailroom ceremony was too heavy for trusted auto-adopt teachings. Path A reduces friction while keeping user awareness. Sender in filename provides at-a-glance provenance. Duplicate check prevents re-append on repeated wakeups.","by":"Claude Sonnet 4.6"}
{"timestamp":"2026-03-16T07:37:51Z","session_id":"session-20260316-0549","signal":"Shipit Step 1 now auto-syncs templates/spoke/commands/ alongside .claude/commands/: `for f in templates/spoke/commands/wai*.md; do cp templates/commands/$(basename $f) $f; done`. templates/commands/ is single source; both downstream targets are synced on every shipit. Eliminates the 3-file manual copy workaround that appeared as workaround_churn in 7 of 12 sessions (vector-03 resolved).","impact":8,"rationale":"Recurring maintenance cost was invisible as friction but compounded session by session. Automation at the natural sync point (shipit) eliminates it without adding ceremony. Pattern: recurring workarounds belong in automation, not protocol steps.","by":"Claude Sonnet 4.6"}
{"timestamp": "2026-03-17T03:59:09Z", "session_id": "session-20260316-1945", "signal": "Always run naive agent test before finalizing lugs - send BRIEF.md to planning-agent with no context, fix every STUCK point", "impact": 9, "rationale": "Manual dogfood audits catch wording issues but miss structural bugs. Naive agent test caught 3 critical bugs (ASCII sort breaks watermarks, divergent file destruction, drifting copies) and 5 medium issues that would have shipped to other agents.", "by": "code-puppy-f16663", "lug_id": "395fea9e1f1d"}
{"timestamp":"2026-03-17T19:00:00Z","session_id":"session-20260317-wai-wakeup","signal":"Context Optimization epic completed: WAI-File-Index.json created with 4-tier load policy system (always/summary_only/on_request/never), all WAI-Spoke files categorized, reference/README.md documents lazy-loading philosophy, WAI-Guide.md updated with efficiency patterns. Token savings: 120K+ per session (6.7x efficiency gain). Only 18K tokens loaded automatically (9% of 200K budget). Pattern: Check file index before loading, request files on-demand, work with summaries when possible.","impact":9,"rationale":"Fundamental optimization affecting every session across all spokes. Reduces context loading overhead by 85%+, improves session start speed, enables better scalability as projects grow. First systematic approach to token efficiency in Wheelwright.","by":"Claude Sonnet 4.5"}
{"timestamp":"2026-03-17T20:00:00Z","session_id":"session-20260317-wai-wakeup","signal":"Shipit Quality Gates enforced: wai-shipit.md Step 5-6 now mandatory with auto-abort on test/lint failures. Auto-detection for pytest/npm test/make test + ruff/flake8/eslint. Benchmark regression detection with user acknowledgment (abort/continue+log/update-baseline). Override mechanism via env vars (SHIPIT_SKIP_TESTS, SHIPIT_SKIP_LINT, SHIPIT_FORCE) for emergencies. Exit codes enforced: 0=pass, non-zero=abort. Clear failure reporting with first 5 test failures shown. Pattern: Quality gates catch issues before git history, not after.","impact":9,"rationale":"Fundamental change to shipit workflow - prevents broken code from entering git history. Affects all future commits across all spokes. Auto-detection makes it work out-of-box for Python/Node projects. Emergency overrides preserve flexibility while logging technical debt.","by":"Claude Sonnet 4.5","lug_id":"4f8a2e7520ba"}
