{"timestamp":"2026-03-18T08:00:00Z","session_id":"session-20260318-0100","signal":"Track Chain Protocol enables portable session continuity across any tool/environment. Users can load track from Claude Code into ChatGPT, continue conversation, generate new track that links to predecessor, then load into Cursor. Creates complete audit trail across conversation chains. Schema: session_metadata field with predecessor linking (session_id, source_file, last_turn, timestamp). Tested: 8/8 scenarios including deep chains (A→B→C), cross-tool continuity, origin sessions.","impact":9,"rationale":"Fundamental capability for conversation portability. Enables users to move between tools without losing context. Critical for AI-assisted work that spans multiple sessions/environments. Production-ready with comprehensive testing.","by":"Claude Sonnet 4.5"}
{"timestamp":"2026-03-18T08:00:01Z","session_id":"session-20260318-0100","signal":"E1-E7 Skill System Migration complete: WAI-Skills.jsonl registry with 24 skills (2 core, 6 advisory, 10 utility, 6 governance). Advisory skills auto-trigger on patterns (complexity gate: 2+ files OR 6+ steps, stewardship: scope drift, context: lazy-loading). Session modes enable user control (execution, interactive, planning, review, deploy). KB migrated: WAI-Guide v1→v2 (archived legacy, slimmed to skill index). Hub distribution ready via skill-system-v1.md.teaching.","impact":9,"rationale":"Transforms Wheelwright from command collection to governed skill system. Enables discovery (registry), stewardship (advisors), evolution (lifecycle management), and distribution (hub teach/learn). Foundation for all future governance features.","by":"Claude Sonnet 4.5"}
{"timestamp":"2026-03-18T08:00:02Z","session_id":"session-20260318-0100","signal":"Build-test-ship workflow: Track Chain Protocol and E1-E7 both implemented with comprehensive testing BEFORE presenting to user. Track Chain: 8/8 test scenarios (schema validation, predecessor detection, chain reconstruction, deep chains, origin sessions, cross-tool, backward compat). E1-E7: 16/16 verification checks (schema, files, modes, advisors). Zero issues found in production validation. Pattern: implement → test exhaustively → commit → report completion.","impact":8,"rationale":"Establishes production-grade quality standard. User requested 'build it, don't tell me about it till it passes testing and is 100% ready for review' - this workflow delivers that. Reduces user review burden, increases confidence in shipped features.","by":"Claude Sonnet 4.5"}
{"timestamp": "2026-03-18T10:44:09.006577+00:00", "session_id": "session-20260318-closeout", "signal": "Teaching reconciliation protocol: Step 3a wakeup now auto-detects already-implemented teachings via 3-tier verification (filename in signals, teaching name in signals, verification files exist). Auto-copies to processed/ folder without confirmation. Eliminates false-positive 'new teachings' on every wakeup when hub teachings are already implemented locally.", "impact": 8, "rationale": "Solves fundamental usability issue affecting all spokes: hub teachings are immutable (can't be moved), so filename-based detection was insufficient. This protocol enables copy-on-reconcile pattern that works with canonical hub structure. Affects all future wakeups across all spokes.", "by": "Claude Sonnet 4.5", "lug_id": "6ed194b4add6"}
